WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.775
A standard view stores a query definition It does
not normally store

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:11.639
a separate snapshot of the result When the view is
queried PostgreSQL

00:00:11.666 --> 00:00:17.691
uses the view definition to access current
underlying data For consumers

00:00:17.915 --> 00:00:21.073
the view behaves like a named relation with columns
and rows
